From: Srinivas Kandagatla <srinivas.kandagatla@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 15:20:12 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 21/22] arm64: dts: qcom: glymur: add analog audio LPASS glue
 and SoundWire IPs

Add the LPASS glue needed to bring up analog audio on Glymur:

  * SoC dtsi
    - lpass_rxmacro and lpass_txmacro codec nodes with their LPASS
      clock inputs (mclk, macro/dcodec votes, npl, va-macro fsgen).
    - lpass_audiocc and lpasscc clock controllers driving the
      SoundWire RX/TX CGCR resets.
    - swr1 (RX @ 0x06a80000) and swr2 (TX @ 0x07630000) SoundWire
      controllers, disabled by default.  Boards choose the topology
      -- mobile-mode uses swr1/swr2 as independent buses; compute-mode
      uses swr2 as the primary and swr1 as its data-only secondary
      (see qcom,primary-controller in the follow-up commit).

  * Board (CRD) dtsi
    - Sound card node with WSA/VA DAI links and DAPM routes for HPH
      playback (IT 41 <- HPHL/HPHR_OUT) and the TX macro <- WCD OT 36
      capture bridge.  WCD9378 compute-mode DAI links and the codec
      node come in the follow-up commit.
    - wcd_default reset pin state on gpio191.

Signed-off-by: Srinivas Kandagatla <srinivas.kandagatla@oss.qualcomm.com>
(cherry picked from commit ff7f453f051258815533378f0ba719237111ec41)
(cherry picked from commit d48341d72ef0b10b3a44a01100112bdd6ec36000)

[jack74: glymur-crd.dtsi hunk dropped (CRD routes, conflicts with the
 k74 CRD DMIC changes); A16 board wiring is a separate commit]
